Z||000006||Heretic||09-23-2001||12:11 AM||||I personally like it with the spoiler. But a lot of the fieros i see without spoilers are hella sweet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://us.ent1.yimg.com/album.yahoo.com/images/muze/album/400/405754_th1.jpg">  CD of the week - Alien Ant Farm - Anthology||||reg||6
Z||000007||FLASHY||09-23-2001||01:46 AM||||To be honest I used to hate the GT's without a wing. But ever since I saw a Ferrari 355 I couldn't believe the resemblance it had to a fiero and started liking the look of GT's without wings. I've even thought about painting my fiero yellow someday and leaving the wing off. You never would have heard me say that in the past. They look more streamline without them. But don't get me wrong wing-lovers, I still love having the wing, especially when I look in my rear view mirror.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I guess in my opinion they look faster with a wing but more exotic without.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flash_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||1
Z||000008||Sootah||09-23-2001||01:55 AM||||I like the fastbacks with and without the wing. But the notchback ABSOLUTELY HAS TO HAVE <B>SOMETHING</B> on it!! Even if it is the luggage rack. (The wing obviously looking better than the rack)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">  <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FLASHY||09-23-2001||02:03 AM||||I agree Sootah. They look a little bare with nothing there.||||reg||1
Z||000010||gargoyle||09-23-2001||02:08 AM||||I have a silver 87 GT with wing but next spring it will become wingless, sort of. I picked up a whaletale  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> like california kid has on his yellow GT. I think it fits the lines a lot better. If I were going to stay with a wing I would go with a thinner and more functional one. I am staying silver though but I am thinking about doing the aero parts in blue. So in the spring I will be selling mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tonker||09-23-2001||02:24 AM||||I find it depends on the colour of your car. Some colours look good with the wing off, other make it look like something is missing.||||reg||1
Z||000012||seadog||09-23-2001||06:53 AM||||I also like the wingless GT, it looks really exotic looking at it from a 3/4 rear view, however from a straight side view, it does look like the rear could be a little more finished. Maybe a one or two inch upturn at the rear decklid hmmm. When I bought the fiero it HAD to have the wing. A couple of years later I removed it to touch-up a small chip. The wife wanted to know how quickly could I  Put That Back On. By the end of the week the wingless look had grown on both of us and I sold the wing, nope no regrets.<P>Richard 86 GT <BR> ||||reg||14
